# Decorative Stainless Steel Sheet — Specification Quick Reference

A practical cheat sheet for architects, interior contractors and procurement teams
specifying decorative stainless steel for commercial interiors.
Maintained by [Ferosteel](https://www.ferosteel.com/) — a decorative stainless
sheet manufacturer exporting from China.

## 1. Grade selection

| Grade | Best for | Corrosion | Cost |
|-------|----------|-----------|------|
| 201 | Dry indoor decorative use only | Moderate | Lowest |
| 304 | General commercial interiors, elevators, wall panels, furniture, ceilings | Good | Balanced |
| 316L | Coastal, humid, pool/spa, chemical-exposed interiors | Best (molybdenum) | Higher |

Rule of thumb: 304 covers ~80% of indoor commercial projects.
Step up to 316L near coastlines.

## 2. Surface finishes

| Finish | Character | Typical use |
|--------|-----------|-------------|
| Hairline / brushed | Directional satin, hides fingerprints | Walls, furniture, elevators |
| Mirror 8K | High reflectivity | Luxury feature walls, ceilings, cabins |
| PVD colored | Gold / rose gold / champagne / black / grey / blue / copper | Any base finish, color on top |
| Etched | Patterned, light/dark texture | Feature walls, elevator backs |
| Embossed / water ripple | 3D texture, reflective ripple | Ceilings, lounge walls |
| Bead blasted | Fine matte | Modern architectural interiors |
| Antique copper | Aged metal look | Boutique, hospitality |

## 3. Thickness ranges

- Decorative cladding: 0.3 – 3.0 mm (typical 0.6 – 1.0 mm over substrate)
- Countertops: 3.0 – 12.0 mm
- Required thickness depends on span, substrate and fixing method —
  not on catalog default.

## 4. Fabrication available

Laser cutting · V-grooving · bending · welding · polishing
→ Ask the shop whether forming happens *before* PVD coating.
(If coating comes first, exposed edges show bare steel.)

## 5. RFQ checklist

- [ ] Grade (201 / 304 / 316L)
- [ ] Thickness
- [ ] Dimensions (sheet size or final panel size)
- [ ] Base finish (hairline / mirror / etched / ...)
- [ ] PVD color or physical sample reference
- [ ] Pattern direction & repeat
- [ ] Quantity
- [ ] Fabrication required (cutting / bending / welding)
- [ ] Destination country / port

## 6. Before mass production

Approve a physical sample under the project's actual lighting.
Color perception shifts with light temperature and viewing angle.

